(jit_monitor.py:141: _fwd_kernel, batch_memcpy_kernel, fused_sigmoid_gating_delta_rule_update_kernel) and the log's own advice is 'consider extending warmup to cover this shape/config'. NUM_WARMUPS=8 with 320 prompts; the first measured window (10:37:34) shows 239.9 gen tok/s, consistent with cold-shape compilation being charged to the measurement. fused_sigmoid_gating_delta_rule_update_kernel is a GDN decode kernel, so its cold compile lands on the decode path itself.\n- expected_impact: 1-3% via warmup coverage (benchmark-side, not server-side)\n- accuracy_risk: none\n- domain_tags: warmup, jit, gdn\n- status: proposed\n- source: runs/baseline/.../server.log 10:37:23 jit_monitor.py:141","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
