{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_a4861364bd941f5d","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\n## Findings\n\nFile-offset note first: the installed file logs at lines 159/501/505; the server log showed 163/505/510 — same code, ~4-line offset (a patched fork at `/opt/envs/wu1w/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/.../qwen_gdn_linear_attn.py` logs at exactly 164/506/510; it adds a `fused_gdn_hip` torch-library shim, but that module is NOT installed — `find_spec('fused_gdn_hip')` is None). All citations below are against the target file.\n\n**1. Decode kernel selection.** `VLLM_GDN_DECODE_KERNEL` env var, choices `{cuda, triton}`, default `\"cuda\"` (`/opt/envs/vllm/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/envs.py:130,1216-1220`), consumed at `qwen_gdn_linear_attn.py:492-505`. \"cuda\" = `torch.ops._C.fused_gdn_decode_post_conv_mtp` (`qwen_gdn_linear_attn.py:532-533, 1750`); on this ROCm wheel that op is not built (verified `hasattr(torch.ops._C, ...) == False`), and since the env var was unset it fell back with the logged reason (`:496-503`) instead of raising. Alternatives within \"triton\": the packed decode FLA kernel `fused_recurrent_gated_delta_rule_packed_decode` (`:489-491, 1270-1282, 1632-1684`, gated by `VLLM_ENABLE_FLA_PACKED_RECURRENT_DECODE`, default 1, `envs.py:129,1210`) vs. the generic `fused_sigmoid_gating_delta_rule_update` (`:1528-1547`). The AITER Triton decode path (`:74-85, 1566-1630`) is unavailable on gfx90a: `are_gdn_triton_kernels_available` is `@if_aiter_supported` requiring `get_cdna_version() > 2` (`_aiter_ops.py:1996-2004,1664-1674`; `platforms/rocm.py:362-371` maps gfx90a→2) plus `VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER` default False (`envs.py:134`); it also requires `gqa_interleaved_layout` (`:1217-1222`), which Qwen3.5-style non-interleaved models don't have. Runtime probe confirmed `GDN_AITER_TRITON_AVAILABLE=False`.\nVerdict: Triton/FLA is the only selectable-and-available decode path here; \"cuda\" is a no-op fallback, and there is no other switch to flip.\n\n**2. State (SSM cache) dtype handling.** The cache tensor `kv_cache[1]` is passed directly to the kernel with its allocation dtype, from `--mamba-ssm-cache-dtype`/`--mamba-cache-dtype` (`gdn/base.py:53-58` → `mamba_utils.py:113-128`, `config/cache.py:129-136`). The kernels read the cache in its native dtype and upcast only on load: `b_h = tl.load(p_h0, ...).to(tl.float32)` (`flash_linear_attention/ops/fused_recurrent.py:120,307`; `fused_sigmoid_gating.py:120`) and write back with `tl.store(p_ht, b_h.to(p_ht.dtype.element_ty))` (`fused_recurrent.py:161,340`; `fused_sigmoid_gating.py:166,170`). No separate internal fp32 state buffer.\nVerdict: the kernel reads/writes the cache dtype directly; fp32 exists only transiently in registers.\n\n**3. Recurrence arithmetic.** The [BV,BK] accumulator is explicitly fp32: `b_h = tl.zeros([BV,BK], dtype=tl.float32)` (`fused_sigmoid_gating.py:102`, `fused_recurrent.py:102`); every decay/delta/output step (`b_h *= exp(b_g)`, `b_v -= tl.sum(b_h*b_k)`, `b_h += b_v[:,None]*b_k`, `b_o = tl.sum(b_h*b_q)`, lines `fused_sigmoid_gating.py:144-153`) runs in fp32, and q/k/v/a/b/A_log/dt_bias are all `.to(tl.float32)` on load. The same is true of the AITER port (`/opt/envs/vllm/lib/python3.12/site-packages/aiter/ops/triton/_triton_kernels/gated_delta_rule/decode/fused_rearrange_sigmoid_gdr.py:101,117,154`).\nVerdict: `bfloat16` ssm cache only narrows the per-token store→load round-trip of S; it does not change the arithmetic — accuracy cost is exactly one bf16 re-quantization of S per decoded token.\n\n**4. Prefill switch.** `--gdn-prefill-backend` / `additional_config[\"gdn_prefill_backend\"]` with choices `flashinfer|triton|cutedsl`, default `auto` (`engine/arg_utils.py:758,1691-1697,2496-2497`; resolution in `_resolve_gdn_prefill_backend` `qwen_gdn_linear_attn.py:93-141`, dispatch `:220-241`). There is no `fused`/`chunk`/`aiter` value. On ROCm gfx90a: `current_platform.is_cuda()` is False for the ROCm platform (`platforms/interface.py:189-190`), so `:117-118` returns \"triton\" for any request; flashinfer needs SM90 or SM10.x+head_k_dim=128+CUDA≥13 (`:127-134`) and cutedsl needs SM10.x (`:130-135, 305-346`).\nVerdict: Triton/FLA chunk is the only viable prefill on gfx90a for head_k_dim=128; the logged \"requested=auto → Triton/FLA\" line (`:158-163`) is correct and unavoidable.\n\n**5. Shape/block-size dependence of decode.** Grid = `(NK=1, NV=cdiv(V,BV), N_seqs*HV)` with `BK=next_pow2(K)=128`, `BV=min(next_pow2(V),32)=32` (`fused_sigmoid_gating.py:208-210,241`; `fused_recurrent.py:195-196,217`); the packed variant adds a Z-split only when `B*HV > 65535` (`fused_recurrent.py:452-455`) — none of this depends on mamba `block_size`. State slots are addressed one page per sequence via `non_spec_state_indices_tensor = block_table_tensor[:, 0]` (`v1/attention/backends/gdn_attn.py:260`) with `state_idx <= 0` (NULL_BLOCK) early-outs (`fused_recurrent.py:299-303`). What ssm dtype does change: per-token HBM traffic is `HV*(V*K)*2*(read+write)*itemsize` (≈0.52 MB vs 1.05 MB per token per layer at HV_local=8, K=V=128 for bf16 vs fp32) and `MambaSpec.page_size_bytes` (`v1/kv_cache_interface.py:677-685`), i.e. fp32 halves the number of state blocks that fit. Spec decode widens conv state by `num_spec` (`mamba_utils.py:258-260`) and adds per-draft-token state block copies; the (unbuilt) fused CUDA path also caps `num_spec <= 8` (`:89,1810`).\nVerdict: kernel grid/tiling is head-count/dim driven and block-size independent; bf16 vs fp32 ssm cache is a pure 2x HBM-bytes + cache-capacity lever with no arithmetic change — making `--mamba-ssm-cache-dtype bfloat16` a bandwidth-only optimization on this decode path.\n\nResult artifact written to `/home/qiba/ROCm.AI/hyperloom/session/Qwen3.8-27B-ABLITERATED-W8A8-gdnint8/20260915T103412Z-bf20aced/runs/specialist/bdfa2a5a13b4422fa31439361d165510/leaf_result.json`."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a6fd8bed1bc052ce7 (use SendMessage with to: 'a6fd8bed1bc052ce7', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 79468\ntool_uses: 50\nduration_ms: 416833</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4f5fa1a2-e349-4774-856c-cb06ca25bfcd","uuid":"d8d5da77-30cc-4acb-8d30-ace8024adc1c","timestamp":"2026-09-15T12:28:22.386Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Read-only investigation in the installed vLLM source at /opt/envs/vllm/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm (v0.28.0+rocm723, gfx90a/MI500-class ROCm).\n\nTarget file: /opt/envs/vllm/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/model_executor/layers/mamba/gdn/qwen_gdn_linear_attn.py (and anything it imports for the DECODE path, e.g. ops under vllm/model_executor/layers/mamba/ops/ and vllm/third_party/flash_linear_attention/ops/).\n\nThe baseline server log printed exactly these lines:\n  [qwen_gdn_linear_attn.py:163] Using Triton/FLA GDN prefill kernel (requested=auto, head_k_dim=128).\n  [qwen_gdn_linear_attn.py:505] Falling back to the Triton GDN decode path: torch.ops._C.fused_gdn_decode_post_conv_mtp is not built\n  [qwen_gdn_linear_attn.py:510] GDN decode kernel: triton\n\nAnswer precisely, quoting file:line:\n1. What GDN decode kernel implementations can be selected (triton vs C++/AITER/other), what env var or flag selects them, and is any alternative actually available/built in this install?\n2. What dtype does the decode kernel read/write for the recurrent state (ssm state / \"state\" or \"S\" buffer)? Does the kernel cast the cache to fp32 internally, or does it read the cache dtype directly? Look for `.to(`, `dtype=`, tl.load on the state tensor.\n3. Is the delta-rule recurrence accumulation done in fp32 registers even when the cache tensor is bf16 (i.e. would --mamba-ssm-cache-dtype bfloat16 only narrow the store/load, or would it change the arithmetic)?\n4. Any existing upstream switch (env var, config field) for GDN prefill kernel choice (e.g. requested=auto values: fla / chunk / fused / cutedsl / aiter) and which ones are viable on ROCm gfx90a for head_k_dim=128?\n5. Anything in the decode path that is obviously shape- or block-size-dependent (e.g. does the mamba page size / ssm dtype change grid sizes or per-step HBM bytes)?\n\nReport concise findings with file:line citations and a one-line verdict per question. Do not attempt edits.","agentId":"a6fd8bed1bc052ce7","agentType":"hyperloom-leaf","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\n## Findings\n\nFile-offset note first: the installed file logs at lines 159/501/505; the server log showed 163/505/510 — same code, ~4-line offset (a patched fork at `/opt/envs/wu1w/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/.../qwen_gdn_linear_attn.py` logs at exactly 164/506/510; it adds a `fused_gdn_hip` torch-library shim, but that module is NOT installed — `find_spec('fused_gdn_hip')` is None). All citations below are against the target file.\n\n**1. Decode kernel selection.** `VLLM_GDN_DECODE_KERNEL` env var, choices `{cuda, triton}`, default `\"cuda\"` (`/opt/envs/vllm/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/envs.py:130,1216-1220`), consumed at `qwen_gdn_linear_attn.py:492-505`. \"cuda\" = `torch.ops._C.fused_gdn_decode_post_conv_mtp` (`qwen_gdn_linear_attn.py:532-533, 1750`); on this ROCm wheel that op is not built (verified `hasattr(torch.ops._C, ...) == False`), and since the env var was unset it fell back with the logged reason (`:496-503`) instead of raising. Alternatives within \"triton\": the packed decode FLA kernel `fused_recurrent_gated_delta_rule_packed_decode` (`:489-491, 1270-1282, 1632-1684`, gated by `VLLM_ENABLE_FLA_PACKED_RECURRENT_DECODE`, default 1, `envs.py:129,1210`) vs. the generic `fused_sigmoid_gating_delta_rule_update` (`:1528-1547`). The AITER Triton decode path (`:74-85, 1566-1630`) is unavailable on gfx90a: `are_gdn_triton_kernels_available` is `@if_aiter_supported` requiring `get_cdna_version() > 2` (`_aiter_ops.py:1996-2004,1664-1674`; `platforms/rocm.py:362-371` maps gfx90a→2) plus `VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER` default False (`envs.py:134`); it also requires `gqa_interleaved_layout` (`:1217-1222`), which Qwen3.5-style non-interleaved models don't have. Runtime probe confirmed `GDN_AITER_TRITON_AVAILABLE=False`.\nVerdict: Triton/FLA is the only selectable-and-available decode path here; \"cuda\" is a no-op fallback, and there is no other switch to flip.\n\n**2. State (SSM cache) dtype handling.** The cache tensor `kv_cache[1]` is passed directly to the kernel with its allocation dtype, from `--mamba-ssm-cache-dtype`/`--mamba-cache-dtype` (`gdn/base.py:53-58` → `mamba_utils.py:113-128`, `config/cache.py:129-136`). The kernels read the cache in its native dtype and upcast only on load: `b_h = tl.load(p_h0, ...).to(tl.float32)` (`flash_linear_attention/ops/fused_recurrent.py:120,307`; `fused_sigmoid_gating.py:120`) and write back with `tl.store(p_ht, b_h.to(p_ht.dtype.element_ty))` (`fused_recurrent.py:161,340`; `fused_sigmoid_gating.py:166,170`). No separate internal fp32 state buffer.\nVerdict: the kernel reads/writes the cache dtype directly; fp32 exists only transiently in registers.\n\n**3. Recurrence arithmetic.** The [BV,BK] accumulator is explicitly fp32: `b_h = tl.zeros([BV,BK], dtype=tl.float32)` (`fused_sigmoid_gating.py:102`, `fused_recurrent.py:102`); every decay/delta/output step (`b_h *= exp(b_g)`, `b_v -= tl.sum(b_h*b_k)`, `b_h += b_v[:,None]*b_k`, `b_o = tl.sum(b_h*b_q)`, lines `fused_sigmoid_gating.py:144-153`) runs in fp32, and q/k/v/a/b/A_log/dt_bias are all `.to(tl.float32)` on load. The same is true of the AITER port (`/opt/envs/vllm/lib/python3.12/site-packages/aiter/ops/triton/_triton_kernels/gated_delta_rule/decode/fused_rearrange_sigmoid_gdr.py:101,117,154`).\nVerdict: `bfloat16` ssm cache only narrows the per-token store→load round-trip of S; it does not change the arithmetic — accuracy cost is exactly one bf16 re-quantization of S per decoded token.\n\n**4. Prefill switch.** `--gdn-prefill-backend` / `additional_config[\"gdn_prefill_backend\"]` with choices `flashinfer|triton|cutedsl`, default `auto` (`engine/arg_utils.py:758,1691-1697,2496-2497`; resolution in `_resolve_gdn_prefill_backend` `qwen_gdn_linear_attn.py:93-141`, dispatch `:220-241`). There is no `fused`/`chunk`/`aiter` value. On ROCm gfx90a: `current_platform.is_cuda()` is False for the ROCm platform (`platforms/interface.py:189-190`), so `:117-118` returns \"triton\" for any request; flashinfer needs SM90 or SM10.x+head_k_dim=128+CUDA≥13 (`:127-134`) and cutedsl needs SM10.x (`:130-135, 305-346`).\nVerdict: Triton/FLA chunk is the only viable prefill on gfx90a for head_k_dim=128; the logged \"requested=auto → Triton/FLA\" line (`:158-163`) is correct and unavoidable.\n\n**5. Shape/block-size dependence of decode.** Grid = `(NK=1, NV=cdiv(V,BV), N_seqs*HV)` with `BK=next_pow2(K)=128`, `BV=min(next_pow2(V),32)=32` (`fused_sigmoid_gating.py:208-210,241`; `fused_recurrent.py:195-196,217`); the packed variant adds a Z-split only when `B*HV > 65535` (`fused_recurrent.py:452-455`) — none of this depends on mamba `block_size`. State slots are addressed one page per sequence via `non_spec_state_indices_tensor = block_table_tensor[:, 0]` (`v1/attention/backends/gdn_attn.py:260`) with `state_idx <= 0` (NULL_BLOCK) early-outs (`fused_recurrent.py:299-303`). What ssm dtype does change: per-token HBM traffic is `HV*(V*K)*2*(read+write)*itemsize` (≈0.52 MB vs 1.05 MB per token per layer at HV_local=8, K=V=128 for bf16 vs fp32) and `MambaSpec.page_size_bytes` (`v1/kv_cache_interface.py:677-685`), i.e. fp32 halves the number of state blocks that fit. Spec decode widens conv state by `num_spec` (`mamba_utils.py:258-260`) and adds per-draft-token state block copies; the (unbuilt) fused CUDA path also caps `num_spec <= 8` (`:89,1810`).\nVerdict: kernel grid/tiling is head-count/dim driven and block-size independent; bf16 vs fp32 ssm cache is a pure 2x HBM-bytes + cache-capacity lever with no arithmetic change — making `--mamba-ssm-cache-dtype bfloat16` a bandwidth-only optimization on this decode path.\n\nResult artifact written to `/home/qiba/ROCm.AI/hyperloom/session/Qwen3.8-27B-ABLITERATED-W8A8-gdnint8/20260915T103412Z-bf20aced/runs/specialist/bdfa2a5a13b4422fa31439361d165510/leaf_result.json`."}],"resolvedModel":"qwen3.8-flash-next","totalDurationMs":416833,"totalTokens":79468,"totalToolUseCount":50,"usage":{"input_tokens":3752,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":73600,"output_tokens":2116,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":7,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":43,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
